== Cost and remaining state
The standard gcd bound is O(M(n) log n) field operations. Charging the native exponentiation-based scalar inversions gives the conservative modular-multiplication bound O(M(n) log n + n log r). The sign-constraint power still costs O(M(n) log r), and source evaluation remains separate. Installed multiplication is Karatsuba; FFT constants and practical crossover thresholds are not claimed.

Root coefficients remain linear in n. Recursive matrices, transition metadata and polynomial temporaries are charged, with conservative O(n log n) workspace rather than a measured RSS figure. Larger-transcript aggregation without full root materialization remains the next mathematical task. No timing panel or cloud work ran; the original4,563-case cohort is unchanged.

